#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# sequence_count

#% text
# `sequence_count(xs, p)` gives the number of non-overlapping runs of `xs` that match the list pattern `p`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Runs do not overlap: `[1, 1, 1]` holds one run `[1, 1]`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
sequence_count([1, 1, 2, 1, 1], [1, 1])
#% output
#= 2

#% cell
sequence_count([1, 1, 1], [1, 1])
#% output
#= 1

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# `count` counts single elements:

#% cell
count([1, 1, 2, 1, 1], 1)
#% output
#= 4

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `sequence_cases`, `count`
